{"step_index":214,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:48:34Z","thinking":"The audio analysis reveals a clear transition point at approximately 00:06:18.00, marked by a significant volume increase from -25.3 dB (silence after the prayer) to -15.9 dB (music and singing). This confirms the identified start of the first song segment. Now, I will use this transition point to accurately identify the boundaries of the subsequent song segments.\n\n\nConfirmed start and end times for all song segments based on the provided timestamps. Considered the user's intent to remove singing while retaining speech. Identified the pre-stream silent segment at the beginning and the need to determine whether to include or exclude it based on user preference. This information suggests creating a timeline where the identified song segments are cut and all other video content is kept. Then create a FCPXML file with this timeline.\n\n\nInitial focus is on generating FCPXML and EDL files for DaVinci Resolve, prioritizing versatility across both free and studio versions. Determined that these formats would achieve the desired editing outcomes without quality loss or re-rendering. Proceeding to ascertain video properties such as file path, duration, frame rate, resolution, and audio parameters, to ensure accurate metadata inclusion in the generated files.\n\nCurrently, the intent is to calculate the 'KEEP' segments, where the audio/video content will be retained.\n\n\nDetermining the exact start time for the initial spoken segment requires clarifying the user's preference regarding the \"hold screen.\"  Two options are considered: include the silent pre-speech segment (starting at 00:00:00) or begin at the actual greeting (00:04:40). All subsequent talking segments must be preserved.\n\nAll identified \"keep\" ranges are listed, which include the opening, all interstitial shares, and the complete remainder of the meeting. The goal is to generate both an EDL and an FCPXML file.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Generate DaVinci Resolve EDL and FCPXML timeline files with the singing segments removed and all talking preserved.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import os\n\nfps = 30\nvideo_file = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - September 13, 2026.mp4\"\nvideo_filename = os.path.basename(video_file)\n\n# Segments to KEEP (Start sec, End sec, Description)\n# We start at 00:04:40 (where opening talking begins) or 00:00:00\nkeep_segments = [\n    (280.0, 378.0, \"Opening Welcome & Prayer\"),          # 00:04:40 - 00:06:18\n    (527.0, 563.0, \"Sharing 1: Power of Christ Risen\"),    # 00:08:47 - 00:09:23\n    (760.0, 1431.0, \"Prayer & Sharing 2: Intercession\"),   # 00:12:40 - 00:23:51\n    (1665.0, 1688.0, \"Sharing 3: Life of Christ\"),        # 00:27:45 - 00:28:08\n    (1799.0, 1810.0, \"Sharing 4: Christ in Saints\"),      # 00:29:59 - 00:30:10\n    (1940.0, 2002.0, \"Sharing 5: Forgiveness & Pit\"),     # 00:32:20 - 00:33:22\n    (2172.0, 7125.0, \"Welcome, Announcements, Sermon\"),   # 00:36:12 - 01:58:45\n]\n\ndef sec_to_tc(sec, frame_rate=30):\n    total_frames = int(round(sec * frame_rate))\n    f = total_frames % frame_rate\n    tot_s = total_frames // frame_rate\n    s = tot_s % 60\n    tot_m = tot_s // 60\n    m = tot_m % 60\n    h = tot_m // 60\n    return f\"{h:02d}:{m:02d}:{s:02d}:{f:02d}\"\n\ndef sec_to_frames(sec, frame_rate=30):\n    return int(round(sec * frame_rate))\n\n# 1. Generate CMX 3600 EDL\nedl_path = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl\"\nwith open(edl_path, \"w\", encoding=\"ascii\") as f:\n    f.write(f\"TITLE: RLCF Sunday No Singing\\n\")\n    f.write(f\"FCM: NON-DROP FRAME\\n\\n\")\n    \n    timeline_frame = 0 # Timeline starts at 01:00:00:00 standard or 00:00:00:00\n    timeline_start_sec = 3600 # 01:00:00:00\n    \n    for idx, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n        dur = src_end - src_start\n        src_in_tc = sec_to_tc(src_start, fps)\n        src_out_tc = sec_to_tc(src_end, fps)\n        \n        rec_in_tc = sec_to_tc(timeline_start_sec + timeline_frame / fps, fps)\n        timeline_frame += int(round(dur * fps))\n        rec_out_tc = sec_to_tc(timeline_start_sec + timeline_frame / fps, fps)\n        \n        # Format CMX 3600 edit line\n        # Event 001 AX V C In Out RecIn RecOut\n        f.write(f\"{idx:03d}  AX       AA/V  C        {src_in_tc} {src_out_tc} {rec_in_tc} {rec_out_tc}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"* FROM CLIP NAME: {video_filename}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"* COMMENT: {desc}\\n\\n\")\n\nprint(f\"Generated EDL: {edl_path}\")\n\n# 2. Generate Final Cut Pro XML (FCPXML v5 / DaVinci Resolve compatible)\nxml_path = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml\"\ntotal_timeline_frames = sum(sec_to_frames(end - start, fps) for start, end, _ in keep_segments)\n\n# Convert file path to file:// URL\nimport urllib.parse\nfile_url = \"file://localhost/\" + urllib.parse.quote(video_file.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\"))\n\nxml_content = f\"\"\"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE xmeml>\n<xmeml version=\"5\">\n  <project>\n    <name>RLCF Sunday No Singing</name>\n    <children>\n      <clip id=\"masterclip-1\">\n        <name>{video_filename}</name>\n        <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n        <rate>\n          <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n          <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n        </rate>\n        <media>\n          <video>\n            <track>\n              <clipitem id=\"clipitem-media-1\">\n                <name>{video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <file id=\"file-1\">\n                  <name>{video_filename}</name>\n                  <pathurl>{file_url}</pathurl>\n                  <rate>\n                    <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                    <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                  </rate>\n                  <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                  <media>\n                    <video>\n                      <samplecharacteristics>\n                        <width>1280</width>\n                        <height>720</height>\n                      </samplecharacteristics>\n                    </video>\n                    <audio>\n                      <samplecharacteristics>\n                        <samplerate>44100</samplerate>\n                        <depth>16</depth>\n                      </samplecharacteristics>\n                      <channelcount>2</channelcount>\n                    </audio>\n                  </media>\n                </file>\n              </clipitem>\n            </track>\n          </video>\n        </media>\n      </clip>\n      <sequence id=\"sequence-1\">\n        <name>RLCF Sunday - Singing Removed</name>\n        <duration>{total_timeline_frames}</duration>\n        <rate>\n          <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n          <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n        </rate>\n        <timecode>\n          <rate>\n            <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n            <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n          </rate>\n          <string>01:00:00:00</string>\n          <frame>{fps * 3600}</frame>\n        </timecode>\n        <media>\n          <video>\n            <format>\n              <samplecharacteristics>\n                <width>1280</width>\n                <height>720</height>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n              </samplecharacteristics>\n            </format>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\n# Build video track clipitems\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"video-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{desc}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n          </video>\n          <audio>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\n# Build audio track 1\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"audio-1-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{desc}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n                <sourcetrack>\n                  <mediatype>audio</mediatype>\n                  <trackindex>1</trackindex>\n                </sourcetrack>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\n# Build audio track 2\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"audio-2-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{desc}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n                <sourcetrack>\n                  <mediatype>audio</mediatype>\n                  <trackindex>2</trackindex>\n                </sourcetrack>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n          </audio>\n        </media>\n      </sequence>\n    </children>\n  </project>\n</xmeml>\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(xml_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(xml_content)\n\nprint(f\"Generated XML: {xml_path}\")\n","Description":"Generate DaVinci Resolve EDL and XML timeline files","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\56930dde-d49e-4d64-b3a0-ddf3ad4cb3e8\\scratch\\generate_resolve_timelines.py","toolAction":"Create generate_resolve_timelines script","toolSummary":"Create generate_resolve_timelines.py"}}]}
