{"step_index":222,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:48:55Z","content":"I have analyzed the full 1 hour 58 minute recording (`RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - September 13, 2026.mp4`) using acoustic feature profiling and speech recognition. \n\nAll **6 singing segments** have been identified and removed, while preserving the **opening welcome**, all **5 interstitial spoken sharings/prayers**, and the **entire remainder of the service** (announcements, children's memory verses, sermon, and closing prayer).\n\n---\n\n### Cut & Edit Breakdown\n\n| Segment / Action | Timecode Range | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **KEPT (Clip 1)** | `00:04:40` $\\rightarrow$ `00:06:18` | **Opening Spoken Welcome & Prayer** (*\"That's one of the things I love about our church...\"*) |\n| ✂️ *CUT OUT* | `00:06:18` $\\rightarrow$ `00:08:47` | *Song 1: \"Come be enthroned on our praise...\"* |\n| **KEPT (Clip 2)** | `00:08:47` $\\rightarrow$ `00:09:23` | **Spoken Sharing 1** (*\"The greatest power that has ever been manifested in the universe...\"*) |\n| ✂️ *CUT OUT* | `00:09:23` $\\rightarrow$ `00:12:40` | *Song 2: \"See what a morning... Christ is risen...\"* |\n| **KEPT (Clip 3)** | `00:12:40` $\\rightarrow$ `00:23:51` | **Spoken Prayer & Intercession** (*\"Let's use this time for personal prayer... In Jesus name, Amen.\"*) |\n| ✂️ *CUT OUT* | `00:23:51` $\\rightarrow$ `00:27:45` | *Song 3: Hymn singing with piano* |\n| **KEPT (Clip 4)** | `00:27:45` $\\rightarrow$ `00:28:08` | **Spoken Sharing 3** (*\"All that we just sang... How shall we live, brothers, sisters?\"*) |\n| ✂️ *CUT OUT* | `00:28:08` $\\rightarrow$ `00:29:59` | *Song 4: \"All to his time, come back unto thee...\"* |\n| **KEPT (Clip 5)** | `00:29:59` $\\rightarrow$ `00:30:10` | **Spoken Sharing 4** (*\"God has a treasure in Heaven, that's Jesus Christ... His treasure here on earth is Christ in saints below\"*) |\n| ✂️ *CUT OUT* | `00:30:10` $\\rightarrow$ `00:32:20` | *Song 5: \"O to tongues of fire...\"* |\n| **KEPT (Clip 6)** | `00:32:20` $\\rightarrow$ `00:33:22` | **Spoken Sharing 5** (*\"...reminds us to not quickly forget our forgiveness from our former sins...\"*) |\n| ✂️ *CUT OUT* | `00:33:22` $\\rightarrow$ `00:36:12` | *Song 6: Worship closing song* |\n| **KEPT (Clip 7)** | `00:36:12` $\\rightarrow$ `01:58:45` | **Announcements, Sunday School Memory Verses, Sermon, Testimonies & Closing Prayer** |\n\n*(Total time trimmed: ~21 minutes of singing removed. Total edited duration: ~1 hr 37 min).*\n\n---\n\n### Ready-to-Use DaVinci Resolve Timeline Files\n\nI have generated two timeline files for you directly in your **Downloads** folder:\n\n1. **`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml`** *(FCPXML format — Recommended)*\n2. **`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl`** *(CMX 3600 EDL format)*\n\n---\n\n### How to Open It in DaVinci Resolve (2 Clicks)\n\n1. Open **DaVinci Resolve** and open your project.\n2. In the top menu, click **File** $\\rightarrow$ **Import** $\\rightarrow$ **Timeline...** (or press `Ctrl + Shift + I`).\n3. Select [`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml`](file:///C:/Users/djtwo/Downloads/RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml) from your Downloads folder.\n4. If Resolve asks to locate media, point it to `RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - September 13, 2026.mp4` in your Downloads folder.\n\nResolve will instantly construct the timeline with all cuts pre-made and all talking sections lined up. Because this links directly to the original video without re-encoding, there is **zero generation loss**, and you can drag any clip edge on the timeline to fine-tune handles if you wish.","thinking":"DaVinci Resolve utilizes the `.xml` or `.edl` files for timeline import. The process involves opening the software, navigating to the file import function within a project, and selecting the desired `.xml` or `.edl` file. This action initiates automatic timeline construction by the application. The software then links the imported timeline directly to the s