{"step_index":238,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:53:55Z","content":"**Yes, absolutely!** Since your source video is 720p (`1280x720`) and you have an **NVIDIA RTX 3050 Ti GPU**, you can upscale it to **1080p Full HD** or even **4K** cleanly.\n\nHere are the best ways to do it in DaVinci Resolve:\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Change Timeline & Scaling Settings *(Works in Free & Studio)*\n\nThis scales the 720p footage up using high-quality bicubic/Lanczos filtering:\n\n1. Click the **Project Settings (gear icon)** in the bottom-right corner of Resolve.\n2. Under **Master Settings** $\\rightarrow$ **Timeline Resolution**:\n   - Change it to **`1920 x 1080 HD`** *(or `3840 x 2160 Ultra HD`)*.\n3. Click on the **Image Scaling** tab on the left:\n   - Change **Resize filter** from *Linear* to **Sharper** (this uses high-quality Lanczos scaling).\n4. Click **Save**.\n\nWhen you go to the **Deliver** page to export, set your export resolution to **`1920 x 1080`** (or 4K).\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: DaVinci Neural Engine \"Super Scale\" *(Studio Version)*\n\nIf you are running **DaVinci Resolve Studio**, it has AI-powered upscaling that runs on your RTX 3050 Ti:\n\n1. In the **Media Pool** (top-left), right-click your video clip: `RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming...`\n2. Select **Clip Attributes**.\n3. Under the **Video** tab, look for **Super Scale**:\n   - Set **Super Scale** to **2x Enhanced** (or **2x**).\n   - Set **Sharpness** to *Medium* or *High*.\n   - Set **Noise Reduction** to *Low*.\n4. Click **OK**.\n\n*Super Scale uses AI tensor cores to hallucinate and reconstruct sharp edges and fine details instead of just stretching pixels.*\n\n---\n\n### 💡 YouTube Tip:\nIf you plan to upload this back to YouTube, **upscaling to 1440p (2560x1440) or 4K** is a well-known trick: \nYouTube automatically gives 1440p and 4K uploads its high-quality **VP9 / AV01 codec** with a much higher bitrate, so it will look significantly cleaner and sharper on YouTube than an original 720p upload!","thinking":"Initial assessment: The user has a 720p video and wants to know about upscaling options. DaVinci Resolve 19 is available along with an RTX 3050 Ti laptop GPU. The hardware should be sufficient for upscaling. DaVinci Resolve likely offers built-in upscaling tools.\n\n\nYes, the RTX 3050 Ti GPU enables effective upscaling within DaVinci Resolve. There are multiple methods available. The first method involves adjusting both timeline and export resolutions within Project Settings to increase the final output size. The second method, available in the Studio version, utilizes the DaVinci Neural Engine for AI-based upscaling, leveraging the GPU for sharp edges and artifact reduction.\n\n\n"}
