{"step_index":246,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:56:43Z","thinking":"Resolve likely defaulted to a `00:00:00:00` start timecode for the MP4 due to the absence of embedded timecode data. The video file being in the Media Pool prior to XML import suggests an automated match should have occurred. The failure to match during XML import requires investigating how Resolve handles timecode synchronization in this specific scenario, given the pre-existing media.\n\n\nThe \"Automatically import source clips into media pool\" setting likely caused Resolve to bypass linking to the existing clips, opting instead to search for them on disk. Two straightforward fixes involve either re-conforming from bins using file names or re-importing the timeline with that option disabled, ensuring the existing clips are used. It's crucial to verify if the clip names in the XML precisely match the file names; if not, the software's conform engine could be using the clip name for matching.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Update XML so that clipitem names match the exact filename in the Media Pool for instant automatic linking.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import os\nimport xml.sax.saxutils as saxutils\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\n\nfps = 30\nvideo_file = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - September 13, 2026.mp4\"\nvideo_filename = os.path.basename(video_file)\n\nkeep_segments = [\n    (280.0, 378.0, \"Opening Welcome and Prayer\"),\n    (527.0, 563.0, \"Sharing 1 Power of Christ Risen\"),\n    (760.0, 1431.0, \"Prayer and Sharing 2 Intercession\"),\n    (1665.0, 1688.0, \"Sharing 3 Life of Christ\"),\n    (1799.0, 1810.0, \"Sharing 4 Christ in Saints\"),\n    (1940.0, 2002.0, \"Sharing 5 Forgiveness and Pit\"),\n    (2172.0, 7125.0, \"Welcome Announcements Sermon\"),\n]\n\ndef sec_to_frames(sec, frame_rate=30):\n    return int(round(sec * frame_rate))\n\nxml_path = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml\"\ntotal_timeline_frames = sum(sec_to_frames(end - start, fps) for start, end, _ in keep_segments)\n\nsafe_video_filename = saxutils.escape(video_filename)\n# Use local Windows path format for FCPXML\nfile_url = \"file://localhost/\" + video_file.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\")\n\nxml_content = f\"\"\"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE xmeml>\n<xmeml version=\"5\">\n  <project>\n    <name>RLCF Sunday No Singing</name>\n    <children>\n      <clip id=\"masterclip-1\">\n        <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n        <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n        <rate>\n          <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n          <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n        </rate>\n        <media>\n          <video>\n            <track>\n              <clipitem id=\"clipitem-media-1\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <file id=\"file-1\">\n                  <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                  <pathurl>{file_url}</pathurl>\n                  <rate>\n                    <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                    <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                  </rate>\n                  <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                  <media>\n                    <video>\n                      <samplecharacteristics>\n                        <width>1280</width>\n                        <height>720</height>\n                      </samplecharacteristics>\n                    </video>\n                    <audio>\n                      <samplecharacteristics>\n                        <samplerate>44100</samplerate>\n                        <depth>16</depth>\n                      </samplecharacteristics>\n                      <channelcount>2</channelcount>\n                    </audio>\n                  </media>\n                </file>\n              </clipitem>\n            </track>\n          </video>\n        </media>\n      </clip>\n      <sequence id=\"sequence-1\">\n        <name>RLCF Sunday - Singing Removed</name>\n        <duration>{total_timeline_frames}</duration>\n        <rate>\n          <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n          <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n        </rate>\n        <timecode>\n          <rate>\n            <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n            <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n          </rate>\n          <string>01:00:00:00</string>\n          <frame>{fps * 3600}</frame>\n        </timecode>\n        <media>\n          <video>\n            <format>\n              <samplecharacteristics>\n                <width>1280</width>\n                <height>720</height>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n              </samplecharacteristics>\n            </format>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"video-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n          </video>\n          <audio>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"audio-1-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n                <sourcetrack>\n                  <mediatype>audio</mediatype>\n                  <trackindex>1</trackindex>\n                </sourcetrack>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"audio-2-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n                <sourcetrack>\n                  <mediatype>audio</mediatype>\n                  <trackindex>2</trackindex>\n                </sourcetrack>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n          </audio>\n        </media>\n      </sequence>\n    </children>\n  </project>\n</xmeml>\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(xml_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(xml_content)\n\nprint(f\"Updated XML: {xml_path}\")\nET.parse(xml_path)\nprint(\"Validation OK!\")\n","Description":"Match clipitem names to filename in XML","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\56930dde-d49e-4d64-b3a0-ddf3ad4cb3e8\\scratch\\generate_resolve_timelines.py","toolAction":"Update XML clip names","toolSummary":"Update generate_resolve_timelines.py"}}]}
