{"step_index":250,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T00:56:57Z","content":"Since the video is **already in your Media Pool**, here is why that happened: \n\nThe option *\"Automatically import source clips into media pool\"* was checked, which forced Resolve to search external drive folders instead of looking at what was **already sitting in your Media Pool**.\n\nYou can link it in seconds using either method below:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Link it right now (No need to re-import)\n1. In your **Media Pool**, right-click the timeline: **`RLCF Sunday - Singing Removed`**.\n2. Select **Timelines** $\\rightarrow$ **Reconform from Bins...**\n3. In the window that appears:\n   - Check **File Name**\n   - Uncheck **Reel Number** (if it is checked)\n   - Click **OK**.\n\nResolve will immediately connect all the cuts on your timeline to the video in your Media Pool!\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Fresh Import (Instant Link)\n1. Delete the current timeline from your Media Pool.\n2. Go to **File** $\\rightarrow$ **Import** $\\rightarrow$ **Timeline...** and pick [`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml`](file:///C:/Users/djtwo/Downloads/RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml).\n3. In the pop-up options window, **UNCHECK**:\n   - `[ ] Automatically import source clips into media pool`\n4. Click **OK**.\n\nBecause that box is unchecked, Resolve will link straight to your video in the Media Pool!","thinking":"When an XML is imported with media already present, the software attempts to locate files on disk if a specific import setting is enabled. It's designed to link these existing clips. To connect the existing media, a specific procedure is required.\n\n\n"}
