{"step_index":260,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T01:00:34Z","thinking":"Resolve likely uses a specific Python version that is incompatible with the user's current environment, which explains the DLL error. The screenshot's error suggests a timecode mismatch, meaning the application can't link the clip because of mismatched timecode extents.\n\nThe error \"failed to link because the timecode extents do not match any clip\" hints at a potential problem with the input video's timecode data versus the expected data. It's likely that the import process relies on specific timecode extents within the file.\n\n\nThe application's import process likely uses the sequence timecode if the file itself lacks explicit timecode information, which creates a mismatch if the sequence timecode is non-zero. The imported clip's timecode is likely interpreted as starting at zero. The application is attempting to reconcile file clip timecode within the larger sequence context, which explains the timecode mismatch error when specific frame ranges are referenced. Inspecting the FCPXML shows how the file and sequence timecodes are defined, confirming this hypothesis.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Fix timecode extents in XML and EDL to 00:00:00:00 so DaVinci Resolve matches the media clip perfectly.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import os\nimport xml.sax.saxutils as saxutils\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport urllib.parse\n\nfps = 30\nvideo_file = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - September 13, 2026.mp4\"\nvideo_filename = os.path.basename(video_file)\n\n# Segments to KEEP (Start sec, End sec, Description)\nkeep_segments = [\n    (280.0, 378.0, \"Opening Welcome and Prayer\"),\n    (527.0, 563.0, \"Sharing 1 Power of Christ Risen\"),\n    (760.0, 1431.0, \"Prayer and Sharing 2 Intercession\"),\n    (1665.0, 1688.0, \"Sharing 3 Life of Christ\"),\n    (1799.0, 1810.0, \"Sharing 4 Christ in Saints\"),\n    (1940.0, 2002.0, \"Sharing 5 Forgiveness and Pit\"),\n    (2172.0, 7125.0, \"Welcome Announcements Sermon\"),\n]\n\ndef sec_to_frames(sec, frame_rate=30):\n    return int(round(sec * frame_rate))\n\ndef sec_to_tc(sec, frame_rate=30):\n    total_frames = int(round(sec * frame_rate))\n    f = total_frames % frame_rate\n    tot_s = total_frames // frame_rate\n    s = tot_s % 60\n    tot_m = tot_s // 60\n    m = tot_m % 60\n    h = tot_m // 60\n    return f\"{h:02d}:{m:02d}:{s:02d}:{f:02d}\"\n\ntotal_timeline_frames = sum(sec_to_frames(end - start, fps) for start, end, _ in keep_segments)\nsafe_video_filename = saxutils.escape(video_filename)\nfile_url = \"file://localhost/\" + urllib.parse.quote(video_file.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\"))\n\n# 1. Update EDL with 00:00:00:00 timeline start\nedl_path = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl\"\nwith open(edl_path, \"w\", encoding=\"ascii\") as f:\n    f.write(\"TITLE: RLCF Sunday No Singing\\n\")\n    f.write(\"FCM: NON-DROP FRAME\\n\\n\")\n    \n    timeline_frame = 0\n    timeline_start_sec = 0 # 00:00:00:00\n    \n    for idx, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n        dur = src_end - src_start\n        src_in_tc = sec_to_tc(src_start, fps)\n        src_out_tc = sec_to_tc(src_end, fps)\n        \n        rec_in_tc = sec_to_tc(timeline_start_sec + timeline_frame / fps, fps)\n        timeline_frame += int(round(dur * fps))\n        rec_out_tc = sec_to_tc(timeline_start_sec + timeline_frame / fps, fps)\n        \n        f.write(f\"{idx:03d}  AX       AA/V  C        {src_in_tc} {src_out_tc} {rec_in_tc} {rec_out_tc}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"* FROM CLIP NAME: {video_filename}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"* COMMENT: {desc}\\n\\n\")\n\nprint(f\"Updated EDL: {edl_path}\")\n\n# 2. Update XML with explicit 00:00:00:00 timecode on both file and sequence\nxml_path = r\"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\Downloads\\RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml\"\n\nxml_content = f\"\"\"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE xmeml>\n<xmeml version=\"5\">\n  <project>\n    <name>RLCF Sunday No Singing</name>\n    <children>\n      <clip id=\"masterclip-1\">\n        <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n        <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n        <rate>\n          <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n          <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n        </rate>\n        <media>\n          <video>\n            <track>\n              <clipitem id=\"clipitem-media-1\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <file id=\"file-1\">\n                  <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                  <pathurl>{file_url}</pathurl>\n                  <rate>\n                    <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                    <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                  </rate>\n                  <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                  <timecode>\n                    <rate>\n                      <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                      <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                    </rate>\n                    <string>00:00:00:00</string>\n                    <frame>0</frame>\n                    <displayformat>NDF</displayformat>\n                  </timecode>\n                  <media>\n                    <video>\n                      <samplecharacteristics>\n                        <width>1280</width>\n                        <height>720</height>\n                      </samplecharacteristics>\n                    </video>\n                    <audio>\n                      <samplecharacteristics>\n                        <samplerate>44100</samplerate>\n                        <depth>16</depth>\n                      </samplecharacteristics>\n                      <channelcount>2</channelcount>\n                    </audio>\n                  </media>\n                </file>\n              </clipitem>\n            </track>\n          </video>\n        </media>\n      </clip>\n      <sequence id=\"sequence-1\">\n        <name>RLCF Sunday - Singing Removed</name>\n        <duration>{total_timeline_frames}</duration>\n        <rate>\n          <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n          <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n        </rate>\n        <timecode>\n          <rate>\n            <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n            <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n          </rate>\n          <string>00:00:00:00</string>\n          <frame>0</frame>\n          <displayformat>NDF</displayformat>\n        </timecode>\n        <media>\n          <video>\n            <format>\n              <samplecharacteristics>\n                <width>1280</width>\n                <height>720</height>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n              </samplecharacteristics>\n            </format>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"video-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n          </video>\n          <audio>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"audio-1-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n                <sourcetrack>\n                  <mediatype>audio</mediatype>\n                  <trackindex>1</trackindex>\n                </sourcetrack>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n            <track>\n\"\"\"\n\ncurr_timeline_frame = 0\nfor i, (src_start, src_end, desc) in enumerate(keep_segments, 1):\n    in_f = sec_to_frames(src_start, fps)\n    out_f = sec_to_frames(src_end, fps)\n    dur_f = out_f - in_f\n    start_f = curr_timeline_frame\n    end_f = curr_timeline_frame + dur_f\n    curr_timeline_frame = end_f\n    \n    xml_content += f\"\"\"              <clipitem id=\"audio-2-clip-{i}\">\n                <name>{safe_video_filename}</name>\n                <duration>{sec_to_frames(7125.88, fps)}</duration>\n                <rate>\n                  <timebase>{fps}</timebase>\n                  <ntsc>FALSE</ntsc>\n                </rate>\n                <start>{start_f}</start>\n                <end>{end_f}</end>\n                <in>{in_f}</in>\n                <out>{out_f}</out>\n                <file id=\"file-1\"/>\n                <sourcetrack>\n                  <mediatype>audio</mediatype>\n                  <trackindex>2</trackindex>\n                </sourcetrack>\n              </clipitem>\n\"\"\"\n\nxml_content += \"\"\"            </track>\n          </audio>\n        </media>\n      </sequence>\n    </children>\n  </project>\n</xmeml>\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(xml_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(xml_content)\n\nprint(f\"Updated XML: {xml_path}\")\nET.parse(xml_path)\nprint(\"XML validation OK!\")\n","Description":"Fix timecode starting offset in XML and EDL","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\djtwo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\56930dde-d49e-4d64-b3a0-ddf3ad4cb3e8\\scratch\\generate_resolve_timelines.py","toolAction":"Update timecode to 00:00:00:00","toolSummary":"Update generate_resolve_timelines.py"}}]}
