{"step_index":264,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T01:00:52Z","content":"That error happened because DaVinci Resolve defaults its timeline start timecode to **`01:00:00:00`**, whereas your MP4 video file starts at **`00:00:00:00`**. Because the timecodes started an hour apart, Resolve couldn't match the frame ranges.\n\n### Fixed!\nI have updated [`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml`](file:///C:/Users/djtwo/Downloads/RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml) and [`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl`](file:///C:/Users/djtwo/Downloads/RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl) so both the file and timeline explicitly start at **`00:00:00:00`**, matching your MP4 clip.\n\n---\n\n### How to load the fixed version:\n\n1. Click **Close** on that Log window.\n2. In your Media Pool (top left), right-click that timeline (`RLCF Sunday - Sin...`) and select **Delete Selected Timelines**.\n3. Go to **File** $\\rightarrow$ **Import** $\\rightarrow$ **Timeline...**\n4. Select [`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml`](file:///C:/Users/djtwo/Downloads/RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.xml).\n5. In the settings dialog:\n   - Verify **Timeline start timecode** now says **`00:00:00:00`**.\n   - **UNCHECK** `[ ] Automatically import source clips into media pool` *(since your video is already in the Media Pool)*.\n6. Click **OK**.\n\n*(Alternatively, you can select [`RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl`](file:///C:/Users/djtwo/Downloads/RLCF_Sunday_No_Singing.edl), which also imports directly).*\n\nThis will link every cut directly to the clip in your Media Pool!","thinking":"The clip linking failure stems from a timecode mismatch between the sequence start time and the MP4 file's actual start time. The XML sequence starts at a non-zero timecode, while the MP4 begins at zero. The MP4's file element within the XML also lacks a explicit timecode.\n\n\n"}
